 of the skps from tartarus  has been spotted  in this district so the entire area was  evacuated  some citizens are still inside this area  so two ketsubutsu hero students have  been dispatched to locate these missing  people  and get them to safety the two hero  students in question are characters  we've met before  during the provisional hero license  exams their names are  shindo and tatami eventually the two of  them are able to locate  the missing civilians who are holed up  together inside a building  shindo and tatami try to convince these  people to follow them to the shelter  but they refuse these people are not  just helpless civilians who are hiding  inside a building  they made the conscious decision not to  evacuate because after everything that  happened  they simply don't trust the heroes to  protect them these citizens feel that  they would be more  vulnerable inside the shelter so they  decided to band together  and make some sort of makeshift  vigilante militia  this group has already managed to take  down some of the criminals who tried  looting their neighborhoods in the past  so they're confident that they can also  protect their hometown against the  villains  shindo tries to explain that taking down  a few looters  is not the same as taking down an skp  from tartarus  but the citizens refused to listen and  the fact that the heroes  sent a couple of kids to protect these  people instead of full-fledged pro  heroes  only underscores the fact that the  heroes are weak and cannot be  trusted i mean the citizens do have a  point here after everything that  happened all the death  and chaos and destruction it's hard to  believe that the heroes know what  they're doing  and the fact that they're sending high  school students into these dangerous  areas  only shows that the heroes are getting  desperate these particular citizens are  more confident in their own collective  abilities than they are in the abilities  of a couple of high school students 