 with excitement as he realizes  that he now has an opportunity to get  revenge on the very person who sent him  to prison  and that is how this intense chapter  ends wow what a great chapter i really  liked that first half with the citizens  who refused to evacuate  because it's showing us to what extent  confidence in the heroes has eroded  the hero society is in such chaos that  entire districts have been evacuated  because of the villain threats  and then you have large groups of people  who are banding together to form  vigilante militias to protect themselves  because they do not trust the heroes  on top of that shindo almost died in  this chapter we have to appreciate the  gravity of that fact  if deku didn't show up in that exact  moment shindo would literally be  dead and yet it was the heroes who sent  him a high school student  into this dangerous situation the heroes  are obviously  short on manpower and they are  absolutely desperate  that is the only explanation for the  fact that they sent high school students  into an area where a major and  incredibly dangerous villain was spotted  in the future other hero students may  not be as lucky as shindo was  in this chapter and if this chaos  continues and if the heroes  keep relying on heroes students to fight  on the front lines  we may end up seeing some hero students  dying this policy of actually sending  high school students into these  dangerous situations  is such a massive shift as far as the  rules of the hero society go  and this really drives home just how  much things have changed since the  beginning of the story  before the events of the war arc sending  high school students into such dangerous  situations would have been  unimaginable but things have changed  drastically  and they may never be the same again  personally  i'm a little surprised that muscular is  just running around on his own  since i would have expected all for one  to recruit him into his personal villain  army since muscular is incredibly strong  and since he was affiliated with the  league of villains before  my guess was that he was going to serve  some sort of higher purpose  for all for one but who knows maybe  muscular's job was to bait deku and the  other big heroes to come out of hiding  and all for one may be watching all of  this  from behind the scenes and getting ready  to strike  either way though whether this is  muscular just being his crazy self or  whether this is part of a larger plan  i am very excited to see a rematch  between muscular  and deku this is going to be crazy  especially with deku's new powers and  his new  badass persona let me know what you guys  think how  awesome is vigilante deku do you think  that he will take  muscular out or is this going to become  a more complicated battle  like for example will other villains and  heroes  end up joining this fight also do you  think that deku  already has access to the quirks of the  second and third one for all user  and is he about to use them against  muscular  leave your feedback down in the comments  below  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more pocono hero content right  here on the channel don't forget to  leave that like  it really helps a lot and if you're new  to anime pro or maybe you just haven't  subscribed yet  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on  all notifications you can also hit me up  on twitter  and instagram at anime uproar  a big thank you to all of our anime  uproar patrons for making videos like  this one possible  special thank you to alpha sigma  disciple  of lord twego himself and i can't forget  our  the one tier patrons the ones who stand  above  all other clans including ingrata  acquired respect pate heffa liam  thompson  algertol dr cortman dustin scarlett  emperor otaku spidey life  baked buddhist tungsten tarcus and yuno  finally thank you also to our pro hero  tier patrons  including the one and only gilgamesh  steel